<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:45Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Major protests in France: Macron convenes student representatives</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229a34415272cef3719eed7c9581e9333033ab5baeac2c0617569b155caa05b3</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:20:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-macron-convenes-student-representatives--222e3ff88ce4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-macron-convenes-student-representatives" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is set to meet with high school pupils whose protests over school conditions have sparked a broader movement. Details by Philippe Moreau-Chevrolet, communication specialist and teacher at Sciences Po.</summary></entry><entry><title>France awaits Moody's verdict: Downgrade widely expected as debt fears grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4bcf11f62818a185f2d7c1e5d6e0db92ce6f04b9289e0d328453ca8c6641591e</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T13:10:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-awaits-moody-s-verdict-downgrade-widely-expected-as-debt-fears-grow--ef94e5636e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-awaits-moody-s-verdict-downgrade-widely-expected-as-debt-fears-grow" /><summary type="html">France's cost of living protests come as the country struggles with its increasing public debt. Concerns over these public finances have pushed the nation's 10-year government bond yield above 5% for the first time since 2002—making borrowing costs higher. Oliver Davis, Professor and Head of the French Department at University College Cork, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>War in the Middle East: Israel launches West Bank operations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93d5c248b58aa7ed8e7cfa37f75a8b45e7bac1a23eef54fc1be008f2c279975f</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:57:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/war-in-the-middle-east-israel-launches-west-bank-operations--85a7b4908438.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/war-in-the-middle-east-israel-launches-west-bank-operations" /><summary type="html">Palestinian militants wounded five Israelis in an attack on Friday before being killed in a shootout with soldiers, leading Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu to order a lockdown in the occupied West Bank days before Israeli elections. Details by Kethevane Gorjestani, FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil's tense presidential run-off campaign feels like a psychological thriller</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:410ec813ff0229f3fe32adce8d02f19602fc24a03bb2d941baac8efb4851fa05</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:45:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller--934b659fa2c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller" /><summary type="html">Insults traded on social media and a combative debate have intensified the pressure ahead of a fiercely contested presidential run-off on Sunday, with only a few points separating leftist pro-union President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Singapore's longevity industry: The quest for eternal youth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c322f12c172e9b03df4b019d3140ed144dca85cab77aedbbc13383f44fb3c055</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:53:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth--7654b61f92cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261023-singapore-s-longevity-industry-the-quest-for-eternal-youth" /><summary type="html">In Singapore, the quest for eternal youth is no longer just a billionaire's fantasy. It's becoming big business. High-tech clinics, longevity labs and specialist companies all promise the same thing: slowing down the ageing process. From continuous metabolic monitoring and genetic testing to supplements and oxygen therapy, every aspect of the body is measured and optimised.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Laurent Nunez holds presser on security arrangements ahead of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60909f75670f83793b1fcfc52693379c43674af2e8e49516fb95ffced5dd3923</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:29:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-french-interior-minister-holds-presser-on-security-arrangements-ahead-of-protests--93a92335ffc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-french-interior-minister-holds-presser-on-security-arrangements-ahead-of-protests" /><summary type="html">French Interior Minister Laurent Nunez held a press conference on security arrangements ahead of upcoming protests. He announced that 70,000 security forces would be mobilised on October 24 to keep order.</summary></entry><entry><title>French authorities ban some student protests after weekend looting and clashes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f70f82a57eb4d4801a14f795a6707c07092c8e5b1c3ad5c55e883cd249d633fe</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:21:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-authorities-ban-some-student-protests-after-weekend-looting-and-clashes--105205cf5651.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-authorities-ban-some-student-protests-after-weekend-looting-and-clashes" /><summary type="html">Dozens of protesters took to the Paris streets on Thursday despite bans on demonstrations ordered in multiple French cities following a weekend of clashes and widespread looting that marked France’s most violent unrest in years.</summary></entry><entry><title>SA faces rising tension as foreign national is killed amid anti-migrant protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a13e1e901b7390bf6e283c1a65a1cd0280bced9faf5d9a375daa60cdeebd15</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:08:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests--97fdf43717d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests" /><summary type="html">South African police are investigating the murder of a foreign national after violent protests by anti-immigrant groups swept through the central business district in Durban. The latest death follows months of violent rallies in which at least 10 foreigners were killed and several other countries on the continent raced to repatriate their people. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson.</summary></entry><entry><title>One killed, four including child injured in drive-by shooting in Paris suburb</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fcebd6659c148e5dcaeafa249d1f6ede9b670468b769c48ef2a48aeb19908cc</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:08:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack--4e9b6abddebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261023-french-prosecutors-investigate-paris-shooting-as-suspected-terror-attack" /><summary type="html">One person was killed Friday and four were injured, including a 12-year-old child, when a man opened fire from a vehicle in the town of Trappes west of Paris, police said. French prosecutors said that they were investigating the shooting as a suspected terrorist attack. At least two of the victims have immigrant backgrounds.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Claude Monet: 'Iris' becomes most expensive artwork sold at auction in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f71b4171b339f0310cb7bb093083a4db48e19914f9a45dc094c7523b30769d83</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:04:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-claude-monet-iris-becomes-most-expensive-artwork-sold-at-auction-in-france--3d0975a83709.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-claude-monet-iris-becomes-most-expensive-artwork-sold-at-auction-in-france" /><summary type="html">"Iris," a monumental painting by Impressionist Claude Monet, sold for 50 million euros ($56 million) in Paris on Thursday, becoming the most expensive artwork ever sold at auction in France.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Some 70,000 security forces will be mobilised for French protests on Saturday, says PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f817a6733e771076c41b94db857942ff1dcaa3075b23cfd23eaeaefaece086d1</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:58:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-macron-meets-with-student-representatives-and-law-enforcement-ahead-of-new-protests--325d4c2058c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261023-macron-meets-with-student-representatives-and-law-enforcement-ahead-of-new-protests" /></entry><entry><title>French authorities call for videos of looting to identify rioters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eeea2e3b55022b9c405b1053e32171b3a035e48c689ce1111e3181a29c3ae27</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:47:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-authorities-call-for-videos-of-looting-to-identify-rioters" /><summary type="html">To identify rioters across France last weekend, French authorities are calling on people who filmed scenes of looting to assist the investigation by handing the videos in. That is an unprecedented decision - one causing debate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Art: Claude Monet's 'Iris' fetches 50M euros at Paris auction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9d4ed14c2bb57b0a664d034d681e90817c328d4cd560d8c80ca62e443d7d757</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:47:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/art-claude-monet-s-iris-fetches-50m-euros-at-paris-auction--a681f6bdda79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/art-claude-monet-s-iris-fetches-50m-euros-at-paris-auction" /><summary type="html">"Iris," a monumental painting by Impressionist Claude Monet, sold for 50 million euros ($56 million) including buyer fees in Paris on Thursday, has become the most expensive artwork ever sold at auction in France.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN searches for new Secretary-General as Antonio Guterres term comes to an end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80608428dcda40c770e29cbcfe121bcd0f6b85a725d13f9b8dfdb6a6ff655f45</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:43:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-un-searches-for-new-secretary-general-as-antonio-guterres-term-comes-to-an-end--f10d2b57be2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-un-searches-for-new-secretary-general-as-antonio-guterres-term-comes-to-an-end" /><summary type="html">Antonio Guterres's term as UN Secretary-General is coming to an end. The international organisation is looking for his replacement. Leading candidates are struggling to secure the support they need. Details from FRANCE 24's correspondent in New York, Jessica Le Masurier.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu orders West Bank closure as attack wounds Israelis before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc5dbf5234512b448cbf241c082665f142a22e0cfd974ba0660c8b1b7e845b1e</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:41:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-netanyahu-orders-west-bank-closure-as-attack-wounds-israelis-before-election--fe9233c95ecb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-netanyahu-orders-west-bank-closure-as-attack-wounds-israelis-before-election" /><summary type="html">Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>French mayors analyze the political crisis as new protests are expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b30a4aa564fba30bc003abb2860188502b2a4529fcbba0dc2b1bc8b84544a83</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:39:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-french-mayors-analyze-the-political-crisis-as-new-protests-are-expected--bbaa8fca2779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-french-mayors-analyze-the-political-crisis-as-new-protests-are-expected" /><summary type="html">French mayors Emmanuel Gregoire of Paris and Benoit Payan of Marseille have analysed the current political crisis in France and the government's choice to impose curfews in several cities to prevent violence in upcoming protests. This comes in the wake of weekend unrest and riots.</summary></entry><entry><title>Across Africa: Ivorian vinyl head's heritage hunt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a78f47dfeb4488ba92e1e442677d482a86fde9ffe657d4bd4dddb93c4b9ddde7</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:27:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt--b506a2325208.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt" /><summary type="html">This week in Across Africa: Ivorian music lover Cédric Kouamé is on a mission to restore 20th-century African vinyl and bring old-school sounds back to modern playlists. Also, 10 years after Cameroon's worst railway disaster, families are still fighting for justice for the 79 people killed. Finally, in São Tomé and Príncipe, we discover how the islands' rich volcanic soils produce some of the world's most distinctive vanilla.</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Olympic fever grips Senegal as Dakar hosts Youth Olympic Games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6971cfbc7e1ce42416a036f4427393aee41341d815931c6f2273c6694b921320</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog--8929ff69c2de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog" /><summary type="html">As Senegal prepares to host the Youth Olympic Games (YOG), the first Olympic event ever organised in Africa, the country is pulling out all the stops to be ready on time. FRANCE 24’s Sarah Sakho and Simon Martin report.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Marseille's European slump continues with defeat to Sturm Graz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:610c3aea530d9fd78d73e013ef1ce563cb95bf9c1e180c753215fc80e732a6a0</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:27:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261023-marseille-s-european-slump-continues-with-defeat-to-sturm-graz--dac8286a5fac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261023-marseille-s-european-slump-continues-with-defeat-to-sturm-graz" /><summary type="html">Marseille conceded their third defeat in three Europa League games on Thursday in Graz, as an early goal was enough to seal the three points for the hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Politics in 'materialist terms': Gen Z in Albania, Italy, France and India protesting for 'fairness'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f3fe65d54b9364aad27ff620f0718761fb961caa3849c4510b50618137f1230</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:04:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/politics-in-materialist-terms-gen-z-in-albania-italy-france-and-india-protesting-for-fairness--feef842897cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/politics-in-materialist-terms-gen-z-in-albania-italy-france-and-india-protesting-for-fairness" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Gökçe Tuncel, Sociologist and post-doctoral researcher associated with the Université Paris-Est Créteil (UPEC). For Tuncel, the wave of youth-led protests across France, Albania, India and Italy reveals more than a succession of localized grievances. It signals the emergence of a political consciousness shaped by material insecurity, institutional disillusionment and an increasingly explicit demand for solidarity and social justice. "What is really striking about this Gen Z movement is how clearly young people see their material conditions," Tuncel observes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Major protests in France: French shop owners brace for more unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc49105cb7b5600f7023a548275ad1d2edd11a02890b289329095b5eb7a05ba9</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:46:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-french-shop-owners-brace-for-more-unrest--f989c41f4f04.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/major-protests-in-france-french-shop-owners-brace-for-more-unrest" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said on Thursday that "illegitimate" protests would be banned in the coming days and blamed "seditious" ultra-left groups and vandals for last weekend's riots and looting.</summary></entry><entry><title>NYT reports plans for fresh strikes on Iran after the US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8de5c7dc5d268e733781f1e027c87b8bb95e682bfa42fe04770b3ce372ecfe25</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:40:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nyt-reports-plans-for-fresh-strikes-on-iran-after-the-us-midterm-elections--22bada901bcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nyt-reports-plans-for-fresh-strikes-on-iran-after-the-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Reza Sayah, our correspondent in Tehran Iran, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ivory Coast: Children face serious health risks from lead in paint</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60f66fe71a1cdd61a9417fbdcefc8335cdea0c894961642056a493e821d4a6ff</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:37:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint--1797f4fd2521.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint" /><summary type="html">Report by Jean Barrère &amp; Guillaume Gougeon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu orders army to prepare for full West Bank closure after attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0b804403c4d2bb4bed19683d31b3a2f9fb70e5351d72219782b431f69c41ec3</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:38:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:35:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-netanyahu-orders-army-to-prepare-for-full-west-bank-closure-after-attack--3d1dfabc7ef3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261023-netanyahu-orders-army-to-prepare-for-full-west-bank-closure-after-attack" /><summary type="html">The office of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu ordered the army to prepare for a full closure of the occupied West Bank Friday after Israeli soldiers shot and killed two men who the military said had launched a "terror attack" near the city of Hebron. Emergency services said five people were injured and evacuated to hospitals.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
